==German==

===Etymology===
A diminutive form pertaining to {{m|de|Knoblauch}}. The ''-f-'' is due to its being derived from dialectal forms. One would expect a {{etyl|nds-de|de}} origin (cf. {{cog|gml|knoflōk}}), but there are also forms with ''-f-'' in some southern German dialects (themselves from an {{etyl|goh|-}} variant {{m|goh|chlovalouh}}). Southern origin is more likely given the regional form {{m|de|Knofel}}, but Low German would have helped to spread the form in the north.

